{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917530510},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from a dataset\n2. Use a census file to get the total US residents\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Express it to four decimal places\n5. Provide one confident sentence\n6. Use tools for any math needed\n7. Not mention unverified facts\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md file, I should:\n1. Check `xorq_semantic_models` first to see if there's a relevant semantic model\n2. Check `xorq_catalog_list_aliases` to see what's already in the catalog\n3. Only ingest data if no existing alias covers it\n4. Use `xorq_select` to get values\n5. Use `xorq_verify` to verify all numbers before stating them\n6. Never state a number I didn't obtain from the catalog\n\nLet me start by:\n1. Checking what's in the catalog\n2. Seeing if I need to ingest these two CSV files\n3. Computing the metric\n4. Verifying everything\n\nLet me first check the semantic models and existing aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the U.S. farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the catalog for existing data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SWju9pAyDTwTQYybnqdfV7","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AqANbvFi4WzxzDSwBiraCX","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"c